IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-vintages`
IMPORT `g7-commencement`
IMPORT `g2-readings`

-- ind-c-tests-commencement-vintages: independent tests (author ind-c) of the staged commencement and of the nine texts (endnotes).
-- Row ids C-nn and V-nn are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md.  Days are Jersey days; instants are built in Europe/Jersey (the encoding's assumed zone).

§ `ind-c fixtures for the endnotes`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-c Article in force` n d MEANS `Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` (`an Article of the Law as now numbered` n) d `the favoured interpretation`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-c Schedule in force` n d MEANS `Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` (`a Schedule to the Law` n) d `the favoured interpretation`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-c original Article in force` n d MEANS `Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` (`an Article of the Law as originally numbered` n) d `the favoured interpretation`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Office of the Minister`
`ind-c Minister on` d MEANS `Endnotes: the office of the Minister on` d `the favoured interpretation`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      h IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
`ind-c Jersey instant` d h m MEANS DATETIME_FROM_DTZ d (TIME_FROM_HMS h m 0) "Europe/Jersey"

