-- V-04, V-07, V-11 rest on the commencement seven days after making (R&O.28/2023 Art 3, R&O.56/2025 Art 2, R&O.102/2026 Art 7(6)): the three Orders reach the Table's dates
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the day an instrument made on a day comes into force 7 days after` (YMD 2023 4 5) `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS YMD 2023 4 12
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the day an instrument made on a day comes into force 7 days after` (YMD 2025 10 9) `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 16
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the day an instrument made on a day comes into force 7 days after` (YMD 2026 9 25) `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS YMD 2026 10 2

§ `ind-c POST-HOC-CERTAIN rows (added after the encoding was opened; each follows from a convention fixed in expectations.md before it was)`

-- C-instants: an instrument commences at the start of its Jersey day.  23:30 UTC on 30 May 2019 is 00:30 on 31 May in Jersey (BST), so R&O.40/2019 is in force.
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office of the Minister at` (DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (YMD 2019 5 30) (TIME_FROM_HMS 23 30 0) "Etc/UTC") `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office of the Minister at` (DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (YMD 2019 5 30) (TIME_FROM_HMS 22 30 0) "Etc/UTC") `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the office of the Minister at` (DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (YMD 2026 10 1) (TIME_FROM_HMS 23 30 0) "Etc/UTC") `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
-- C-instants: a question of a DATE alone on 27 February 2024 refuses only where the 09:30 change decides it; the Comptroller and the Dormant Bank Accounts words do not change that day.
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller on` (YMD 2024 2 27) `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the Dormant Bank Accounts openings of Schedule 1 are in force on` (YMD 2024 2 27) `the favoured interpretation`


§ `Moved from ind-c-tests-disagree.l4 (POST-HOC: written after the author opened the encoding): D1 holds since the repair of G7 (R1)`


-- src:876 | Parts 1 to 3, Articles 32, 38, 39, 40, 42, 43 and 44 and
-- src:877 | the Schedules, in force 21 November 2014;
-- src:878 | Parts 4, 5, 7, 8 (other than Article 32), Article 37 in
-- src:879 | force 1 May 2018 (R&O.17/2018);
-- src:880 | Remainder in force 1 January 2019 (R&O.17/2018).
-- src:917 | 41
-- src:918 | spent, omitted
-- src:725 | Part 9
-- src:726 | Miscellaneous and Final Provisions
-- src:727 | 37 Offences by corporate and other bodies
-- R&O.17/2018 Article 2 brings into force on 1 January 2019 every provision not brought in by the original Article 44(2) or by its own Article 1.  The original Article 41
-- (Table of Renumbered Provisions, src:917-918) stood between the original 40 and 42, after the Part 9 heading (src:725), so Part 9 as enacted held it, and it came into force on
-- 1 January 2019.  The encoding itself puts the original 41 in Part 9 (`the Part of the Article originally numbered`) and in stage 3, but computes a Part's stages from the PRESENT
-- Articles only, so Part 9 has two stages and, on its own reading F7.9 A (a Part is in force when all its Articles are), is wholly in force from 1 May 2018.
#ASSERT `Commencement: the stages in which the unit was brought into force` (`a Part of the Law` 9) `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS LIST `stage 1: 21 November 2014`, `stage 2: 1 May 2018`, `stage 3: 1 January 2019`
#ASSERT NOT `Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` (`a Part of the Law` 9) (YMD 2018 6 1) `the favoured interpretation`
